The default-off `--additional-axioms` option also exposes existing closed identities for concrete native integer function-call actuals through local verification assumptions. It preserves original arguments and checks, deduplicates numerals within each emitted assumption, and emits them in numerical order. It adds no module-wide literal inventory or top-level literal identities, and leaves shared function/type axioms, symbolic/real/boxed arguments, pruning and solver settings unchanged.
